    "title": "TV network set for Georgia football game vs. Missouri but kickoff time TBD - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Marc Weiszer ,\n3 days ago\nGeorgia football’ s final SEC home game of the season now has a TV network assigned.\nThe Bulldogs will play Missouri on Nov. 14 on ABC.\nThe kickoff time for the game from Sanford Stadium will be determined after this Saturday's games.\nThe SEC announced Monday that the game will either be at 3:30 p.m. or 7:30 p.m.\nABC will chose from Texas-LSU and Missouri- Georgia for those TV windows.\nGeorgia has not had a night home game this season after playing Alabama and Texas at home last season and at home at night against Tennessee and Georgia Tech in 2024.\nIt will play its second night game on the road Saturday at Ole Miss in a 7:30 p.m. game.\n\"There's nothing I can do about it,\" coach Kirby Smart said Monday. \"It's not a decision I get to make. There's a lot of things that I wanted fixed or corrected in our league before that. That's not a priority. We play on the road at night because we've been a higly-ranked team all those years.\"\nSmart said Georiga hasn't had as many marquee matchups at home.\n\"Let's be honest, we never play Florida at home,\" he said. \"That's one of our premier matchups that lands in the 3:30 all the time. ...I don't really get into the conspiracy theories. Everybody else does. I worry about playing the game.\"\nThe Bulldogs and Tigers will play for the first time since the 2023 season when Georgia won 30-21 in Athens.\nGeorgia has won 10 straight against Missouri since a 41-26 loss in 2013 in Athens.\nMisouri is No. 19 in the coaches poll this week. The Tigers are 6-2 overall and 3-2 in the SEC.\nThe Tigers are coming off a 34-10 win at Arkansas Saturday and host Texas Saturday.\nGeorgia is 7-1 and 5-1 in the SEC.\nThe Bulldogs play at No. 12 Ole Miss after beating Florida 27-8 Saturday in Atlanta.\nThis article originally appeared on Athens Banner-Herald: TV network set for Georgia football game vs. Missouri but kickoff time TBD\nAdd to Preferred Sources\n1",
    "summary": "Georgia football’ s final SEC home game of the season now has a TV network assigned. The SEC announced Monday that the game will either be at 3:30 p.m. or 7:30 p.m. ABC will chose from Texas-LSU and Missouri- Georgia for those TV windows. The Bulldogs and Tigers will play for the first time since the 2023 season when Georgia won 30-21 in Athens. Georgia has won 10 straight against Missouri since a 41-26 loss in 2013 in Athens. This article originally appeared on Athens Banner-Herald: TV network set for Georgia football game vs. Missouri but kickoff time TBD",
